ance\" based on water/petroleum with trimmed impeller; they do not state any motor power (kW/hp) or motor speed (rpm) rating. Therefore the documents do not contain the motor size and speed, and it cannot be confirmed whether the 7.5 kW 1450 rpm motor in stock is suitable.\n\n{\"answer\": null, \"not_present\": true}"}}}
{"qid": "c05", "family": "c", "split": "dev", "method": "M3", "model": "glm", "answer": {"method": "M3", "model": "glm", "final": {"answer": "The item directly downstream of E-2-1 in the process flow is control valve FV-2-2 (a Fisher ET globe valve, per the fisher-et-d100022x012 datasheet). Its available seal and ring materials and temperature capabilities are: 2-piece valve plug seal — disk of PTFE (-73 to 204°C / -100 to 400°F) with backup ring of fluorocarbon (-18 to 204°C / 0 to 400°F), ethylene-propylene (-40 to 232°C / -40 to 450°F), or nitrile (-40 to 71°C / -40 to 160°F for air and hydrocarbons, -40 to 82°C / -40 to 180°F for other compatible fluids); seal ring of carbon-filled PTFE (-73 to 232°C / -100 to 450°F). Spring-loaded valve plug seal — seal ring of PTFE with an N10276 spring (-73 to 232°C / -100 to 450°F), or PTFE/graphite with an R30003 spring (-73 to 316°C / -100 to 600°F), with anti-extrusion rings of PEEK (not a limiting factor); PEEK anti-extrusion rings with a spring-loaded PTFE seal extend the temperature limits to 316°C / 600°F for non-oxidizing service and 260°C / 500°F for oxidizing service.", "not_present": false}, "outcome": "ANSWERED", "route": ["context_rag+chunks"], "cypher": [], "sources": [{"document_id": "fisher-et-d100022x012", "pages": [22, 12, 4, 20, 5, 2, 14, 21, 11, 7]}, {"document_id": "flowserve-worcester-f51-f52", "pages": [7]}, {"document_id": "rosemount-3051-00813-0100-4001", "pages": [68]}], "latency_s": 20.34418470005039, "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 17667, "completion_tokens": 2982, "cost_usd": 0.0004094886, "spent_usd": 0.0004091486, "n_calls": 2, "n_cached": 1, "models": ["qwen/qwen3-embedding-8b", "z-ai/glm-5.3-flash"]}, "trace": {"chunks": [{"document_id": "fisher-et-d100022x012", "page": 22, "score": 0.7017}, {"document_id": "fisher-et-d100022x012", "page": 12, "score": 0.6793}, {"document_id": "fisher-et-d100022x012", "page": 4, "score": 0.6732}, {"document_id": "fisher-et-d100022x012", "page": 20, "score": 0.6718}, {"document_id": "fisher-et-d100022x012", "page": 5, "score": 0.6639}, {"document_id": "flowserve-worcester-f51-f52", "page": 7, "score": 0.663}, {"document_id": "fisher-et-d100022x012", "page": 2, "score": 0.6623}, {"document_id": "fisher-et-d100022x012", "page": 14, "score": 0.6556}, {"document_id": "fisher-et-d100022x012", "page": 21, "score": 0.6548}, {"document_id": "rosemount-3051-00813-0100-4001", "page": 68, "score": 0.6496}, {"document_id": "fisher-et-d100022x012", "page": 11, "score": 0.6465}, {"document_id": "fisher-et-d100022x012", "page": 7, "score": 0.6451}], "prompt_chars": 47839, "reply": "{\"answer\": \"The item directly downstream of E-2-1 in the process flow is control valve FV-2-2 (a Fisher ET globe valve, per the fisher-et-d100022x012 datasheet). Its available seal and ring materials and temperature capabilities are: 2-piece valve plug seal — disk of PTFE (-73 to 204°C / -100 to 400°F) with backup ring of fluorocarbon (-18 to 204°C / 0 to 400°F), ethylene-propylene (-40 to 232°C / -40 to 450°F), or nitrile (-40 to 71°C / -40 to 160°F for air and hydrocarbons, -40 to 82°C / -40 to 180°F for other compatible fluids); seal ring of carbon-filled PTFE (-73 to 232°C / -100 to 450°F). Spring-loaded valve plug seal — seal ring of PTFE with an N10276 spring (-73 to 232°C / -100 to 450°F), or PTFE/graphite with an R30003 spring (-73 to 316°C / -100 to 600°F), with anti-extrusion rings of PEEK (not a limiting factor); PEEK anti-extrusion rings with a spring-loaded PTFE seal extend the temperature limits to 316°C / 600°F for non-oxidizing service and 260°C / 500°F for oxidizing service.\", \"not_present\": false}"}}}
